---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalNotice from '../components/LegalNotice.astro';
import { PRIVACY_VERSION, facts, longDate, operator, processors, retentionChoices } from '../lib/site';

const overseas = processors.filter((p) => p.region !== 'australia-southeast1');
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What AlgoMinutes collects, why, who processes it and where, how long it's kept, and your rights."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Version {PRIVACY_VERSION} · last updated {longDate(PRIVACY_VERSION)}</p>
    <LegalNotice />

    <p>
      This policy explains how {operator.name} (ABN {operator.abn}, "we", "us") handles personal information in
      AlgoMinutes: the app, this website and the service behind them. We follow the Australian Privacy Principles
      in the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth), and, where they apply to you, the EU and UK GDPR and US state privacy
      laws such as California's.
    </p>

    <h2 id="summary">The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We collect what AlgoMinutes needs to work: your account, your recordings and the notes made from them.</li>
      <li>We don't sell your information, show you ads, or track you across other apps and websites.</li>
      <li>Your notes and recordings are stored in {facts.primaryRegionLabel}. Some processing happens outside Australia; <a href="#processors">the table below</a> says where.</li>
      <li>We don't use your recordings or notes to train AI models.</li>
      <li>You can delete any note, or your whole account, at any time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
    <h3>Your account</h3>
    <p>
      When you sign in with Apple or Google we receive an account ID, your email address and, if the provider shares
      it, your name. If you use AlgoMinutes as a guest, we create an anonymous account ID and nothing else. We also
      record when you accepted these documents, and which versions.
    </p>
    <h3>Your recordings and notes</h3>
    <p>
      The audio you record or import, and what AlgoMinutes makes from it: transcripts, summaries, action items,
      decisions, chapters, speaker names you add, and the search index. The questions you ask about your notes are
      processed to answer them, and aren't saved to your account.
      Text you scan from a document or photo is used to create a note the same way. Your recordings contain the
      voices of the people you record; see <a href="#others">People you record</a>.
    </p>
    <h3>How you use the app</h3>
    <p>
      A small set of product events tied to your account, such as "first recording completed" or "plan screen
      viewed", so we can understand whether AlgoMinutes works for people. They don't contain your recordings or note
      content, and we don't use any third-party analytics or advertising tools.
    </p>
    <h3>Support messages</h3>
    <p>What you send us from Help &amp; Support or by email, with your app version, device type and, if you choose, a note's reference.</p>
    <h3>Device and diagnostic information</h3>
    <p>
      Your device's push token, so we can tell you when a note is ready. Crash reports from the app. Server records
      of requests and errors, which carry account and note IDs but are designed to exclude your recordings and note
      content.
    </p>
    <h3>Subscriptions</h3>
    <p>
      When subscriptions go on sale, your plan and its status. Apple handles payment in the App Store, and Stripe on
      the web; we never receive your card details. Nothing is sold during the beta.
    </p>

    <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide AlgoMinutes: transcribing and summarising your recordings, keeping your notes in sync, search and chat, and notifications.</li>
      <li>To keep it working and secure: fixing faults, preventing abuse, and enforcing usage limits.</li>
      <li>To answer your support requests.</li>
      <li>To improve AlgoMinutes, using product events and the feedback you send us. Not your recordings or notes.</li>
      <li>To meet our legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR, we rely on performing our contract with you for the service itself, and on our legitimate
      interests for security, reliability and product improvement.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ai">AI processing</h2>
    <p>
      AlgoMinutes uses Google Cloud's speech and AI models to transcribe and summarise your recordings. Card numbers and
      similar identifiers are removed from transcripts before they're stored, and from transcript text before it's sent
      to an AI model to summarise, search or answer a question. Audio is sent as recorded: for a short recording, the
      model transcribes the audio itself. The models process your content only to produce your results. We don't use your content to train AI models, and our providers' terms
      don't allow them to use it to train theirs. AI output can be wrong: check anything important against the
      recording.
    </p>

    <h2 id="processors">Who processes your information, and where</h2>
    <p>These service providers process personal information on our behalf, under contract, only to provide AlgoMinutes:</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">What for</th><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Where</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {processors.map((p) => (
            <tr id={`processor-${p.id}`}>
              <th scope="row">{p.service}</th>
              <td data-label="What for">{p.purpose}</td>
              <td data-label="What">{p.data}</td>
              <td data-label="Where">{p.where}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 id="overseas">Information sent outside Australia</h3>
    <p>
      Your notes and recordings are stored in {facts.primaryRegionLabel}. The following services may process
      information in other countries, including the United States: {overseas.map((p) => p.service).join('; ')}.
      We choose providers that protect information to a standard comparable to the Australian Privacy Principles,
      and, for information from the EU or UK, use the safeguards those laws require, such as standard contractual
      clauses.
    </p>

    <h2 id="sharing">When we share information</h2>
    <p>We don't sell or rent personal information, and we don't share it for advertising. We disclose it only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>to the service providers above, to run AlgoMinutes;</li>
      <li>when you ask us to, for example by exporting a note (share links are not available yet);</li>
      <li>when the law requires it, or to protect people's safety or our legal rights;</li>
      <li>to a buyer of our business, who would have to keep this policy's promises.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Notes and recordings:</strong> until you delete them. In Settings → Data retention you can have notes deleted automatically after {retentionChoices()}.</li>
      <li><strong>The copy on your phone:</strong> a recording stays on your device only until its upload is confirmed.</li>
      <li><strong>Your account:</strong> until you delete it. Deleting it deletes everything in it at once.</li>
      <li><strong>Backups:</strong> deleted information is removed from our backups within {facts.backupWindowDays} days.</li>
      <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> {facts.logRetentionDays} days.</li>
      <li><strong>Records of deletions and usage:</strong> a record that an account or note was deleted (IDs only, no content) for 30 days, and records of processing usage for 90 days, to prevent abuse and control costs.</li>
      <li><strong>Payment records,</strong> once subscriptions are sold: as long as tax law requires, without your recordings or notes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="others">People you record</h2>
    <p>
      If you're recorded by an AlgoMinutes user, the recording belongs to their account and we process it on their
      behalf. You must be told before you're recorded; our <a href="/terms">Terms</a> require it. You can ask the
      person who recorded you to delete it, or contact us at <a href={`mailto:${operator.privacy}`}>{operator.privacy}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="rights">Your rights and choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access and export:</strong> your notes are in the app, and you can export any note.</li>
      <li><strong>Correction:</strong> edit a note's title, summary and speaker names in the app, or ask us.</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> delete a note, or your account in Settings → Delete my account. <a href="/delete-account">Other ways to delete your account</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> turn them off in your device's settings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may also have the right to object to or restrict our processing, to data
      portability, and to withdraw consent. California residents have the right to know, delete and correct their
      personal information, and we don't sell or share it as those laws define. We won't treat you differently for
      using these rights. To use any of them, email <a href={`mailto:${operator.privacy}`}>{operator.privacy}</a>;
      we may need to confirm it's your account. We reply within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
    <p>
      Information is encrypted in transit and at rest, access to it is limited to the systems and people who need it,
      and every request is checked against your account. No system is perfectly secure; if a data breach is likely to
      cause you serious harm, we'll tell you and the regulator as the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
    <p>
      AlgoMinutes isn't for children. You must be at least 13, and old enough where you live to agree to our Terms
      yourself. If you believe a child has given us personal information, contact us and we'll delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      When we change this policy we update its version and date above. Before a significant change takes effect,
      we'll tell you in the app or by email.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact and complaints</h2>
    <p>
      {operator.name}, {operator.locality}. Email <a href={`mailto:${operator.privacy}`}>{operator.privacy}</a>.
      If you're not satisfied with our response to a privacy complaint, you can contact the Office of the Australian
      Information Commissioner (<a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au">oaic.gov.au</a>), or the data protection authority
      where you live.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
